# CVE-2022-24448

## Description

The NFSv4 protocol allows a client to open a file with the O_CREAT flag set, but without the O_TRUNC flag set. If the file does not exist, the server will create it with the default permissions. If the file does exist, the server will open it with the permissions of the existing file.

## Impact

An attacker can use this vulnerability to create a file with the default permissions, and then use the file to execute arbitrary code.

